# PROFILE.example — the {{tokens}} used in this skill (host-bound values)

The skill text carries DOCTRINE and references every host-bound value by
token. The filled values live in YOUR install, not in this repo. Copy this
file, fill every token, and keep it beside your pipeline instance file.

The skillpipe pipeline already consumes an instance file with overlapping
keys (`skill-foundry/templates/PROFILE.example`) — where a token below
shares a name, it is the SAME value.

```
# The house-repo checkout (the main worktree, on main). This skill's own
# repo — CONVENTIONS.md, README.md, tools/lint_skills.py live here.
REPO_DIR=/abs/path/to/hermes-skills

# Hermes' home dir for this install (profiles, state.db, kanban DB under it).
HERMES_HOME=/abs/path/to/.hermes

# The directory holding the pipeline role playbooks / card canonical bodies
# (e.g. <REPO_DIR>/skill-foundry/references).
CARDS_DIR=/abs/path/to/skill-foundry/references

# The GitHub slug of THIS house repo (gh --repo form).
REPO=<owner>/hermes-skills

# The slug of the fleet repo Hermes' home is checked out from (the OTHER
# skills scope; see the scope trap in SKILL.md). Only if you have one.
FLEET_REPO=<owner>/Hermes

# The profile that operates the pipeline (kicks off cards, owns decisions).
OPERATOR=<operator-profile>

# The profile recorded as creator on dispatch cards.
CREATED_BY=<creator-profile>

# Who runs the role cards. Single-runner install: one profile name.
# Role-isolated install: a role=profile map (author=…, audit=…, …) —
# see skill-foundry/templates/PROFILE.example for the exact ASSIGNEE
# syntax the dispatcher consumes.
ASSIGNEE=<role=profile map or single profile>

# Model ids for the two tiers used by the pipeline (mid = drafting roles,
# high = profile default for judging roles). Values are whatever your
# gateway serves.
MID_MODEL=<your-mid-tier-model-id>
HIGH_MODEL=<your-high-tier-model-id>

# The dedicated gateway key identity the pipeline roles share (attribution
# off the operator's chat key). Name/identity only — the key VALUE is never
# written into any tracked file.
REVIEW_KEY=<dedicated-review-key-identity>

# The host serving the web-access-style service facades referenced in
# references/webaccess-deployment-2026-08.md. Only if you run one.
SERVICE_HOST=<your-service-hostname>
```

## Which files carry which tokens

Computed with `grep -rhoE '\{\{[A-Z_]+\}\}' <file> | sort -u` per file -
recompute after any edit; this map is the audit of the "only declared
tokens present" gate (the registry is the block above):

- `SKILL.md` - ASSIGNEE, CREATED_BY, FLEET_REPO, HERMES_HOME, HIGH_MODEL, MID_MODEL, OPERATOR, REPO, REPO_DIR, REVIEW_KEY.
- `references/host-neutral-doctrine-extraction-2026-09.md` - REPO_DIR.
- `references/linter-rules.md` - REPO_DIR.
- `references/litellm-keys-and-kanban-pinning-2026-09.md` - ASSIGNEE, HERMES_HOME, HIGH_MODEL, MID_MODEL, OPERATOR, REPO_DIR, REVIEW_KEY, SERVICE_HOST.
- `references/sibling-promotion-2026-08.md` - HERMES_HOME, REPO_DIR.
- `references/skills-hub-tap-distribution-2026-08.md` - HERMES_HOME, OPERATOR, REPO, REPO_DIR.
- `references/webaccess-deployment-2026-08.md` - HERMES_HOME, REPO_DIR, SERVICE_HOST.
- `CARDS_DIR` is consumed by the pipeline instance env (the dispatcher
  reads it from the profile), not by the skill prose.
- `${HERMES_SKILL_DIR}` in SKILL.md is NOT an instance token - it is the
  Hermes runtime marker for this skill's own install directory.
